We will build a simple **"Task Manager"** app where you can add tasks and view them.

### Prerequisites
*   Node.js installed (v14 or higher).
*   A code editor (VS Code recommended).

---

### Part 1: Project Structure
Create a folder named `my-app` and set up two subfolders: `client` (React) and `server` (Node/Express).

```bash
mkdir my-app
cd my-app
mkdir client
mkdir server
```

---

### Part 2: The Backend (Node & Express)
This will handle the API logic and store data in memory (for simplicity).

1.  **Initialize the server:**
    ```bash
    cd server
    npm init -y
    npm install express cors nodemon
    ```

2.  **Create `server/index.js`:**
    ```javascript
    const express = require('express');
    const cors = require('cors');
    const app = express();
    const PORT = 5000;

    // Middleware
    app.use(cors()); // Allow React to talk to this server
    app.use(express.json());

    // Dummy Data Store (In-memory)
    let tasks = [
        { id: 1, text: "Learn Node.js", completed: false },
        { id: 2, text: "Build a React App", completed: true }
    ];

    // API Routes

    // 1. Get all tasks
    app.get('/api/tasks', (req, res) => {
        res.json(tasks);
    });

    // 2. Add a new task
    app.post('/api/tasks', (req, res) => {
        const { text } = req.body;
        if (!text) return res.status(400).json({ error: "Text is required" });

        const newTask = {
            id: Date.now(),
            text: text,
            completed: false
        };

        tasks.push(newTask);
        res.status(201).json(newTask);
    });

    // Start Server
    app.listen(PORT, () => {
        console.log(`Server running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
    });
    ```

3.  **Run the server:**
    ```bash
    npx nodemon index.js
    ```
    *You should see: "Server running on http://localhost:5000"*

